<title>INDIA: India eases import curbs on tyres, some fertlisers.</title>
<headline>India eases import curbs on tyres, some fertlisers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Commerce Ministry said on Monday that it shifted tyres and some fertilisers from a restricted list of imports to a list of freely importable items.</p>
<p>In a list of 542 items whose imports have been liberalised under a new five-year export-import policy unveiled earlier on Monday, the ministry listed tyres and NP (nitrogen-phosphorus) and PK (phosphorus-potassium) grade fertilisers.  </p>
<p>The list said &quot;tyres of motor cars, motor cycles, scooters, tractors (and) including used and retreaded tyres and rubber tubes&quot; were now freely importable.</p>
<p>The list also included chewing gum, cornflakes, prunes, jewellery boxes and sewing machines among items that could be freely imported.</p>
</text>
